Exactly one independent Fraction saved-evidence checker is proposed, with a fixed 180-second wall timeout and no adaptive retry. It is written after the sealed analytical and full source reviews, but before any successful target_001 residual details or scientific output were viewed. No new theorem or physical validation is claimed.

Inputs must later be bound to a completed immutable author bundle. Until root explicitly authorizes execution and supplies that binding, do not invoke record_check.py or import/run check_saved_evidence.py. The template is deliberately unbound. A metadata-only source freeze may parse the AST and hash/copy sources; that is not checker execution.

The check includes exact Fraction reconstruction of 128-term arctangent bounds, Machin/512-bit rounding, integer phase branches, degree 256 scalar exponential interval arithmetic and analytic pads, exact projectors, complete root and direct actual-time target. It checks all 32 new endpoint as the chronological product of its24 saved slot matrices; all padded y/G coordinates, all 32 inverse-map/midpoint/nearest-displacement/domain steps; and the final block and every M-power record, complete residual with S^2 normalization, analytic beta allowance, scalar, duration, schedule and resource ledger.

